 Initial ns;result;buff;was;parms
⍝ 1. Create the needed references
⍝ 2. Set global `DEVELOPMENT` depending on user decision (if not running in batch mode)
⍝ 3. Create two namespaces with (very little) content
⍝ 4. Create two Cider projects from those two namespaces
⍝ 5. Initialize both Cider projects as local Git repositories

 A←APLTreeUtils2
 F←FilesAndDirs
 G←APLGit2←##.APLGit2

 'There is no APLGit2 in ⎕SE?!'Assert 9=⎕SE.⎕NC'APLGit2'
 ∆DevelopmentWas←{0=⍵.⎕NC'DEVELOPMENT':¯1 ⋄ ⍵.DEVELOPMENT}⎕SE.APLGit2
 :If ns.batchFlag
     ⎕SE.APLGit2.⎕EX'DEVELOPMENT'
 :Else
     ⎕SE.APLGit2.DEVELOPMENT←~1 CommTools.YesOrNo'Run code in ⎕SE when a user command (rather than #.APLGit2) ?'
 :EndIf

 ⍝ Make it plain which code the user commands are about to execute: a green run against
 ⍝ a stale installed package would not tell us anything. Note that the version numbers
 ⍝ of the two may well match, because a build does not have to be followed by a change.
 :If {0=⍵.⎕NC'DEVELOPMENT':0 ⋄ ⍵.DEVELOPMENT}⎕SE.APLGit2
     ⎕←'*** User commands will execute the code in #.APLGit2.APLGit2 (the project itself)'
 :Else
     ⎕←'*** User commands will execute the INSTALLED package ⎕SE.APLGit2, version ',⎕SE.APLGit2.Version
     ⎕←'    Execute #.APLGit2.Admin.Make 1 in case that is not what you want to test!'
 :EndIf

 ∆LINK_NOTIFY_WAS←⎕SE.Link.NOTIFY
 ⎕SE.Link.NOTIFY←0
 ∆TempDir←F.GetTempSubDir'Git_Tests'
 3 ⎕MKDIR ∆Folder1←G.F.EnforceSlash ∆TempDir,'/NoBlanks'
 3 ⎕MKDIR ∆Folder2←G.F.EnforceSlash ∆TempDir,'/Has Blanks'
 3 ⎕MKDIR ∆Folder3←G.F.EnforceSlash ∆TempDir,'/StagedAndUnTracked'

 'Proj_1'#.⎕NS''
 #.Proj_1.(⎕IO ⎕ML)←1
 #.Proj_1.⎕FX↑'r←WhoAmI' 'r←''Proj_1'''
 (∆Folder1,'/cider.config')⎕NCOPY ##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/cider.config.1'
 result←⎕SE.UCMD'Cider.CreateProject ',∆Folder1,' #.Proj_1 -acceptConfig -noEdit -batch -ignoreUserExec'
 {}∆Initialize ∆Folder1
 (⊂'r←Hello' 'r←''world''')⎕NPUT ∆Folder1,'/APLSource/help.aplf'
 ∆Folder1 G.Add''
 buff←'Function added'G.Commit ∆Folder1
 (⊂'r←Hello' 'r←''World''')⎕NPUT(∆Folder1,'/APLSource/help.aplf')1
 ∆Folder1 G.Add''

 'Proj_2'#.⎕NS''
 #.Proj_2.(⎕IO ⎕ML)←1
 #.Proj_2.⎕FX↑'r←WhoAmI' 'r←''Proj_2'''
 (∆Folder2,'/cider.config')⎕NCOPY ##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/cider.config.2'
 result←⎕SE.UCMD'Cider.CreateProject "',∆Folder2,'" #.Proj_2 -acceptConfig -noEdit -batch -ignoreUserExec'
 {}∆Initialize ∆Folder2
 (⊂'r←Hello2' 'r←''Galaxy''')⎕NPUT ∆Folder2,'/APLSource/help2.aplf'

 'Proj_3'#.⎕NS''
 #.Proj_3.(⎕IO ⎕ML)←1
 #.Proj_3.⎕FX↑'r←WhoAmI' 'r←''Proj_3'''
 (∆Folder3,'/cider.config')⎕NCOPY ##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/cider.config.3'
 result←⎕SE.UCMD'Cider.CreateProject "',∆Folder3,'" #.Proj_3 -acceptConfig -noEdit -batch -ignoreUserExec'
 {}∆Initialize ∆Folder3
 (⊂'r←Hello2' 'r←''Galaxy''')⎕NPUT ∆Folder3,'/APLSource/help2.aplf'
 {}∆Folder3 G.U.RunGitCommand'add ',∆Folder3,'/APLSource/help2.aplf'
 (⊂'r←Hello3' 'r←''Virgo''')⎕NPUT ∆Folder3,'/APLSource/help3.aplf'
 {}∆Folder3 G.U.RunGitCommand'add ',∆Folder3,'/APLSource/help3.aplf'
 (⊂'r←Hello3' 'r←''Virgo Cluster''')⎕NPUT(∆Folder3,'/APLSource/help3.aplf')1
 (⊂'r←Hello4' 'r←''Universe''')⎕NPUT ∆Folder3,'/APLSource/help4.aplf'
 #.Proj_3.⎕FX↑'r←WhoAmI' '⍝ Really!' 'r←''Proj_3'''
 {}⎕SE.Link.Add ⎕SE.Link.GetFileName'#.Proj_3.WhoAmI'

 ⍝ Proj_4 is a ready-made fixture rather than something built here: it carries a Git history,
 ⍝ a second branch, a file in the root of the project, two files with the same name in two
 ⍝ different folders, and a file that is not APL source. See TestData/CiderProject4.zip.
 ⍝ Note that the committer identity is part of that ZIP, so commits can be made in the copy.
 ∆Folder4←G.F.EnforceSlash ∆TempDir,'/CiderProject4'
 3 ⎕MKDIR ∆Folder4
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo ∆Folder4
 parms←⎕SE.Cider.CreateOpenParms''
 parms.folder←∆Folder4
 parms.batch←1
 parms.watch←'ns'
 {}⎕SE.Cider.OpenProject parms
⍝Done
